// Modder-added anomaly types (GRA-98 / v0.5.0 survey rework).
//
// Loads into `SurveyAnomalyRegistry::modder_anomalies` (see
// `src/survey/data.rs`, GRA-79 PR-A scaffold). The nine hardcoded
// anomaly types in `AnomalyType` are always known to the binary
// and are NOT in this file:
//
//   WaterIceDeposit, HydratedSilicates, MethanePlume, TholinSignature,
//   MagneticAnomaly, RadioactiveHotspot, FossilMicrobeSignature,
//   CryovolcanicFeature, UnidentifiedReflectance
//
// See SURVEY_REWORK.md §[Anomalies and Discoveries] for the canonical
// set, effects, and the coolness-vs-effect split (coolness is
// independent of the gameplay unlock — a `fossil_microbe_signature` is
// top-tier coolness for media coverage but is a research unlock, not
// a building unlock).
//
// Field reference (mirrors `ModderAnomalyDef` in `data.rs`):
//   `id`                — stable RON id (snake_case; matches
//                         `AnomalyType::ron_id` convention)
//   `display_name`      — UI label (≤ 32 chars preferred)
//   `description`       — one-line dossier tooltip
//   `discovery_method`  — which `SurveyMethod` is most likely to
//                         surface this anomaly (drives the per-mission
//                         discovery roll; secondary methods can also
//                         surface with lower probability)
//   `coolness`          — "coolness" weight for media coverage, in
//                         [0.0, 1.0]. Independent of gameplay effect
//                         per SURVEY_REWORK §[Coolness weighting].
//
// Modder rebalance: adjust `coolness` to bias the media narrative
// toward/away from this anomaly; pick a more accessible
// `discovery_method` to make the anomaly easier to find.
//
// v0.5.0 ships with zero modder anomalies — this file exists so the
// modder path is exercisable from day one.
(
    modder_anomalies: [
    ],
)
